00:10:55.963 --> 00:10:58.360
then you can start to change your habits

00:10:58.360 --> 00:11:00.260
and your actions and your,

00:11:00.260 --> 00:11:04.520
you can dismantle your
unhealthy defense mechanisms,

00:11:04.520 --> 00:11:06.633
and you know, I'm not great at it.

00:11:07.950 --> 00:11:10.440
I've kind of gone away from the Enneagram.

00:11:10.440 --> 00:11:13.380
I haven't been reading a
lot about it in a few years,

00:11:13.380 --> 00:11:17.080
but it was nice to kind
of get a refresher on it.

00:11:17.080 --> 00:11:20.020
Let's go quickly through all of the types.

00:11:20.020 --> 00:11:20.853
- Okay.

00:11:20.853 --> 00:11:22.524
- But I mean, 'cause we're just going

00:11:22.524 --> 00:11:23.720
to talk about my type in your type today,

00:11:23.720 --> 00:11:27.600
but I'm sure people want
to hear and you know,

00:11:27.600 --> 00:11:29.170
there's quizzes and you can go to the,

00:11:29.170 --> 00:11:30.250
you can go to the website,

00:11:30.250 --> 00:11:34.430
and you can start to read
these books and type yourself.

00:11:34.430 --> 00:11:35.730
It's going to take a little bit more work

00:11:35.730 --> 00:11:39.660
than just the one liner that
I'm going to read right now.

00:11:39.660 --> 00:11:43.760
But I'll just go in numeric order.

00:11:43.760 --> 00:11:45.800
Not because that puts me first,

00:11:45.800 --> 00:11:48.520
just because, I mean, I am a one.

00:11:48.520 --> 00:11:50.420
Type one is called the reformer.

00:11:50.420 --> 00:11:52.850
Some people might call
it the perfectionist.

00:11:52.850 --> 00:11:57.850
One book that we'll refer to
calls the one the machine,

00:11:57.990 --> 00:11:59.363
which I kinda like that.

00:12:00.210 --> 00:12:02.270
The rational, idealistic type.

00:12:02.270 --> 00:12:05.270
Principled, purposeful, self-controlled,

00:12:05.270 --> 00:12:08.093
and perfectionistic.

00:12:09.040 --> 00:12:12.560
Type two, you got the helper.

00:12:12.560 --> 00:12:15.650
That's the caring, interpersonal type.

00:12:15.650 --> 00:12:20.650
Demonstrative, generous,
people-pleasing, and possessive.

00:12:21.610 --> 00:12:22.540
Jessie is a type two.

00:12:22.540 --> 00:12:26.090
- This is my wife, which we
can talk about next week.

00:12:26.090 --> 00:12:29.230
- Type three, you've got the achiever.

00:12:29.230 --> 00:12:30.063
That is you, Rhett.

00:12:30.063 --> 00:12:30.896
- This is me.

00:12:30.896 --> 00:12:35.896
- Do you like any of the other
names besides the achiever?

00:12:36.260 --> 00:12:38.530
- Well, the same book, "Millenneagram",

00:12:38.530 --> 00:12:40.620
which we will recommend later,

00:12:40.620 --> 00:12:42.610
calls this the winner.

00:12:42.610 --> 00:12:43.758
I like that.

00:12:43.758 --> 00:12:44.591
(laughing)

00:12:44.591 --> 00:12:47.430
- The success oriented, pragmatic type.

00:12:47.430 --> 00:12:52.430
Adaptive, excelling,
driven, and image conscious.

00:12:52.500 --> 00:12:53.460
- Can you tell?

00:12:53.460 --> 00:12:55.080
- Type four.

00:12:55.080 --> 00:12:57.500
You've got the individualist.

00:12:57.500 --> 00:12:59.770
The sensitive, withdrawn type.

00:12:59.770 --> 00:13:04.770
Expressive, dramatic,
self-absorbed, and temperamental.

00:13:06.288 --> 00:13:09.320
Type five, the investigator.

00:13:09.320 --> 00:13:12.290
The intense cerebral type.

00:13:12.290 --> 00:13:17.290
Perceptive, innovative,
secretive, and isolated.

00:13:17.490 --> 00:13:19.965
Type six, the loyalist.

00:13:19.965 --> 00:13:23.149
This is my wonderful wife Christy.

00:13:23.149 --> 00:13:26.840
The committed, security oriented type.

00:13:26.840 --> 00:13:31.810
Engaging, responsible,
anxious, and suspicious.

00:13:33.490 --> 00:13:36.593
Type seven, the enthusiast.

00:13:37.670 --> 00:13:39.610
The busy, fun loving type.

00:13:39.610 --> 00:13:44.610
Spontaneous, versatile,
distractable, and scattered.

00:13:46.390 --> 00:13:48.940
Type eight, the challenger.

00:13:48.940 --> 00:13:51.020
The powerful dominating type.

00:13:51.020 --> 00:13:56.020
Self-confident, decisive,
willful, and confrontational.

00:13:56.410 --> 00:13:59.020
Type nine, wrapping things up.

00:13:59.020 --> 00:14:01.210
You've got the peacemaker.

00:14:01.210 --> 00:14:03.380
The easygoing, self-effacing type.

00:14:03.380 --> 00:14:08.160
Receptive, reassuring,
agreeable, and complacent.

00:14:08.160 --> 00:14:13.160
- Now there's a couple of ways
to figure out what you are

00:14:14.302 --> 00:14:17.320
and the one way is the test.

00:14:17.320 --> 00:14:19.220
What I will say about the test is like

00:14:20.160 --> 00:14:22.110
the section called the RHETI.

00:14:22.110 --> 00:14:23.940
R-H-E-T-I.

00:14:23.940 --> 00:14:27.570
It's an acronym for something
from the Enneagram Institute

00:14:27.570 --> 00:14:31.230
has been evaluated to
be like 72% accurate.

00:14:31.230 --> 00:14:32.063
So in other words.

00:14:32.063 --> 00:14:33.150
- I don't think I ever took it.

00:14:33.150 --> 00:14:35.930
- So I took that one and
there's some other free ones

00:14:35.930 --> 00:14:37.630
that you can take online,

00:14:37.630 --> 00:14:40.820
and you're, you might not always score.

00:14:40.820 --> 00:14:43.790
I usually like 90% of the time,

00:14:43.790 --> 00:14:45.630
three will be the thing that hits,

00:14:45.630 --> 00:14:47.130
that pings the highest, right?

00:14:48.210 --> 00:14:50.560
But another way to sort of figure out

00:14:50.560 --> 00:14:54.670
what you are in addition to
the test is to read in depth

00:14:54.670 --> 00:14:57.310
about each one and see
which one resonates the most

00:14:57.310 --> 00:14:58.860
with you and I would go as far.

00:14:58.860 --> 00:15:03.110
I think the way that my
wife put it is the one

00:15:03.110 --> 00:15:05.400
where it feels like
they're reading your mail.

00:15:05.400 --> 00:15:06.650
You know what I'm saying?

00:15:07.763 --> 00:15:09.230
- You might start to get
a little embarrassed.

00:15:09.230 --> 00:15:10.200
- You're going to have a little bit

00:15:10.200 --> 00:15:12.340
of shame and embarrassment,

00:15:12.340 --> 00:15:15.330
some self-consciousness that is associated

00:15:15.330 --> 00:15:18.680
with the negative qualities of each type.

00:15:18.680 --> 00:15:21.060
It's really those negative qualities

00:15:21.060 --> 00:15:22.710
that you you begin to feel that,

00:15:22.710 --> 00:15:23.600
oh, that's me.

00:15:23.600 --> 00:15:24.433
Oh, you got me.

00:15:24.433 --> 00:15:25.550
Yeah, you called me out.

00:15:25.550 --> 00:15:27.461
When I read about three,

00:15:27.461 --> 00:15:31.470
it's clear as day that that's what I,

00:15:31.470 --> 00:15:33.138
and I think you feel very strongly

00:15:33.138 --> 00:15:35.190
in the same way about the one.

00:15:35.190 --> 00:15:36.340
Now some people might not,

00:15:36.340 --> 00:15:38.010
it might be like, I, and again,

00:15:38.010 --> 00:15:39.900
this isn't science, it's not science.

00:15:39.900 --> 00:15:42.210
This is an observational thing

00:15:42.210 --> 00:15:44.280
that just kind of helps
you think about yourself.

00:15:44.280 --> 00:15:46.530
So don't feel too
discouraged if you're like,

00:15:46.530 --> 00:15:49.900
I can't really figure
this out in an afternoon.

00:15:49.900 --> 00:15:50.850
Maybe it's obvious for you,

00:15:50.850 --> 00:15:51.683
maybe it's not,

00:15:51.683 --> 00:15:53.160
but just be patient with it

00:15:53.160 --> 00:15:55.120
if this is something
that you want to pursue.

00:15:55.120 --> 00:15:56.700
- So let's dig into our numbers,

00:15:56.700 --> 00:15:59.260
but first let's promote some merch.

00:15:59.260 --> 00:16:01.570
I got this mug sitting here.

00:16:01.570 --> 00:16:03.290
You want to travel,

00:16:03.290 --> 00:16:04.800
you want to stay hydrated,

