and that's why it's about
being at a Mexican resort

00:48:07.100 --> 00:48:10.410
because I was at a Mexican
resort at the time.

00:48:10.410 --> 00:48:12.380
And it was like, and again.

00:48:12.380 --> 00:48:13.930
- You have to be doing something.

00:48:13.930 --> 00:48:15.377
- If I don't do that.

00:48:15.377 --> 00:48:16.742
- You have to be achieving something.

00:48:16.742 --> 00:48:17.575
- If I choose to be like, you know what?

00:48:17.575 --> 00:48:18.450
Today I'm not writing a song.

00:48:18.450 --> 00:48:19.460
I'm not thinking about,

00:48:19.460 --> 00:48:20.930
I'm not contemplating a project.

00:48:20.930 --> 00:48:22.620
I'm not trying to be a better me.

00:48:22.620 --> 00:48:23.770
I'm just being.

00:48:23.770 --> 00:48:26.250
Again, that's the ultimate
thing for a three is,

00:48:26.250 --> 00:48:28.120
stop doing and start being.

00:48:28.120 --> 00:48:30.500
Learn how to be, not do.

00:48:30.500 --> 00:48:32.560
Very difficult for me to do

00:48:32.560 --> 00:48:35.980
because the moment that
I don't do anything,

00:48:35.980 --> 00:48:39.730
I get this, it feels like
the world is caving in.

00:48:39.730 --> 00:48:41.430
Even this past weekend,

00:48:41.430 --> 00:48:43.013
I spent like an afternoon.

00:48:44.290 --> 00:48:49.003
I watched a movie and then I
kinda just napped on Saturday.

00:48:49.003 --> 00:48:49.878
- Yeah.

00:48:49.878 --> 00:48:51.803
- There was like a four hour
window where it was like,

00:48:51.803 --> 00:48:53.520
it was a movie and then a nap.

00:48:53.520 --> 00:48:54.510
At the end of that I was like,

00:48:54.510 --> 00:48:56.511
I feel horrible.

00:48:56.511 --> 00:48:57.561
What could I have,

00:48:57.561 --> 00:48:59.090
what else could I have
done in that four hours?

00:48:59.090 --> 00:48:59.923
I could have like,

00:48:59.923 --> 00:49:02.440
I could have figured
something out creatively.

00:49:02.440 --> 00:49:05.100
- Well, this is what I did this weekend.

00:49:05.100 --> 00:49:06.330
Were you done with your thought, though?

00:49:06.330 --> 00:49:07.163
- Yeah.

00:49:08.026 --> 00:49:10.310
Well, I want to come back
to the wings in a second

00:49:10.310 --> 00:49:11.360
'cause the wing,

00:49:11.360 --> 00:49:13.170
but I want to hear what you gotta say.

00:49:13.170 --> 00:49:17.857
- Yeah, for me this
weekend, it was, you know,

00:49:19.016 --> 00:49:23.690
I was vacuuming the vents.

00:49:23.690 --> 00:49:25.400
- Yeah, the vents, they get dirty.

00:49:25.400 --> 00:49:26.980
- Because you look up
there and you can start

00:49:26.980 --> 00:49:28.070
to see that boy, they're dirty,

00:49:28.070 --> 00:49:29.370
and I would take them down.

00:49:29.370 --> 00:49:31.240
I realized there was
so much more I could do

00:49:31.240 --> 00:49:33.175
to vacuum inside of the vent.

00:49:33.175 --> 00:49:34.295
- Yeah, you can go all
the way up in there.

00:49:34.295 --> 00:49:35.170
- That type of stuff.

00:49:35.170 --> 00:49:36.465
When I was done with all that,

00:49:36.465 --> 00:49:38.770
I realized that the vacuum
cleaner was really dirty.

00:49:38.770 --> 00:49:43.440
So I disassembled the vacuum
cleaner and cleaned all of it.

00:49:43.440 --> 00:49:48.051
The thing about ones is we can relax

00:49:48.051 --> 00:49:51.663
if we can manage to put things
in just the right order.

00:49:52.860 --> 00:49:54.350
We can have this sense of wellbeing

00:49:54.350 --> 00:49:57.450
when things are are put in their place.

00:49:57.450 --> 00:49:58.306
Like oh, I've cleaned and the thing

00:49:58.306 --> 00:50:01.570
that I cleaned with is now totally clean,

00:50:01.570 --> 00:50:03.370
so now I can relax.

00:50:03.370 --> 00:50:05.040
But if I just cleaned the vents

00:50:05.040 --> 00:50:07.150
and I made my vacuum cleaner dirty,

00:50:07.150 --> 00:50:10.670
well I've created a problem
and that's not made right yet,

00:50:10.670 --> 00:50:13.000
so I couldn't chill out.

00:50:13.000 --> 00:50:16.000
Now this is a trap, of course.

00:50:16.000 --> 00:50:18.431
But I do know that sometimes

00:50:18.431 --> 00:50:20.870
when I'm cleaning or organizing,

00:50:20.870 --> 00:50:22.140
those things make me feel better

00:50:22.140 --> 00:50:25.020
because they give me
that sense of control,

00:50:25.020 --> 00:50:29.340
which is associated with
achieving perfection

00:50:29.340 --> 00:50:30.384
in my own mind.

00:50:30.384 --> 00:50:35.384
Control is really for me
like, nailing perfection.

00:50:36.310 --> 00:50:37.143
- Yeah, yeah.

00:50:37.143 --> 00:50:41.780
- So it's not about whether it's out

00:50:41.780 --> 00:50:43.307
of my control or in my control.

00:50:43.307 --> 00:50:45.680
It's like, it's whether the,

00:50:45.680 --> 00:50:49.677
I can achieve a result
with control and there's,

00:50:49.677 --> 00:50:52.580
you know, there's plenty
of things that I will not,

00:50:52.580 --> 00:50:55.840
I get very sensitive to signing up

00:50:55.840 --> 00:51:00.840
for things if I don't know what,

00:51:01.190 --> 00:51:05.380
if I don't know how to get to
the end goal of perfection.

00:51:05.380 --> 00:51:06.872
Like if it's, if it's open-ended

00:51:06.872 --> 00:51:09.480
or if I feel like it's a big commitment

00:51:09.480 --> 00:51:10.960
and I'm not going to be able to,

00:51:10.960 --> 00:51:12.765
if I get 80% or 70%,

00:51:12.765 --> 00:51:14.540
even if it's a friendship.

00:51:14.540 --> 00:51:17.597
Remember that story I told
about the guy who was just like,

00:51:17.597 --> 00:51:21.840
he was just a friend who wanted
to continue to be a friend,

00:51:21.840 --> 00:51:22.790
ad I broke up with him

00:51:22.790 --> 00:51:24.090
because I didn't feel like

00:51:24.963 --> 00:51:26.400
I could be a good enough friend to him?

00:51:26.400 --> 00:51:30.740
So I like preemptively
just broke up with the guy.

00:51:30.740 --> 00:51:34.550
I mean, that's what was behind it.

00:51:34.550 --> 00:51:37.427
- Well, and this is another
area where the threes

00:51:37.427 --> 00:51:38.480
and the ones are so alike.

00:51:38.480 --> 00:51:40.870
In fact, the three one combo

00:51:40.870 --> 00:51:42.910
which we'll talk more about next week,

00:51:42.910 --> 00:51:45.030
there's actually a nickname
for the three one combo.

00:51:45.030 --> 00:51:46.490
- Oh don't tell, don't tell yet.

00:51:46.490 --> 00:51:47.380
I don't know.

00:51:47.380 --> 00:51:48.380
- I don't know what it is.

00:51:48.380 --> 00:51:49.213
- Okay.

00:51:49.213 --> 00:51:51.840
- But basically it's the combo of numbers

00:51:51.840 --> 00:51:54.280
that will accomplish the most
if you put them together.

00:51:54.280 --> 00:51:55.113
- Ooh.

00:51:55.113 --> 00:52:00.113
- Because they're both
ultimately super committed

00:52:00.480 --> 00:52:02.330
to results.

00:52:02.330 --> 00:52:03.660
And again, like, okay,

00:52:03.660 --> 00:52:05.540
so the one, like, what you're saying is,

00:52:05.540 --> 00:52:08.730
you're hesitant to enter into a situation

00:52:08.730 --> 00:52:11.217
if you don't feel like you're
going to be able to do it

00:52:11.217 --> 00:52:13.160
and you're going to be able to control it.

00:52:13.160 --> 00:52:17.180
A three will gladly
very, they will sign up.

00:52:17.180 --> 00:52:18.380
We will get right in.

00:52:18.380 --> 00:52:19.580
We have no idea.

00:52:19.580 --> 00:52:21.170
We haven't been educated in this area.

00:52:21.170 --> 00:52:22.060
We've never done it before.

00:52:22.060 --> 00:52:22.893
It doesn't matter.

00:52:22.893 --> 00:52:23.860
We're jumping in.

00:52:23.860 --> 00:52:25.866
The moment that we begin to believe

00:52:25.866 --> 00:52:28.810
that we will not achieve,

00:52:28.810 --> 00:52:30.120
that's when we bail.

00:52:30.120 --> 00:52:30.953
Most threes.

00:52:30.953 --> 00:52:33.794
- And for me, I cannot bail.

00:52:33.794 --> 00:52:36.420
So it's like, if I sign up for it,

00:52:36.420 --> 00:52:37.830
I feel like I have to do it.

00:52:37.830 --> 00:52:38.663
So it's like.

00:52:38.663 --> 00:52:40.150
- So I think that again, this,

00:52:40.150 --> 00:52:45.150
the three one combo is
that I will convince you

00:52:45.260 --> 00:52:47.080
to jump into something

00:52:48.050 --> 00:52:51.380
and then I've got this
pathological confidence

00:52:51.380 --> 00:52:53.770
that we will be able to
figure it out and do it.

00:52:53.770 --> 00:52:56.890
And then once you set your mind to it,

00:52:56.890 --> 00:53:00.260
now we're a team, you know?

00:53:00.260 --> 00:53:02.750
So it ends up like, again,

00:53:02.750 --> 00:53:03.610
we've we kind of talked,

00:53:03.610 --> 00:53:04.740
before we understood the Enneagram,

00:53:04.740 --> 00:53:07.970
we talked about it with
like the analogy of like,

00:53:07.970 --> 00:53:10.980
you got one guy who gets the ball rolling

00:53:10.980 --> 00:53:13.135
and you got the other guy
who keeps the ball rolling.

00:53:13.135 --> 00:53:14.151
- A starter and a finisher.

00:53:14.151 --> 00:53:17.710
- That is how it manifests
itself a lot as three to one.

00:53:17.710 --> 00:53:19.920
Now, interestingly as this relates to,

00:53:19.920 --> 00:53:21.440
I want to talk about
the wings a little bit.

00:53:21.440 --> 00:53:26.440
So an aspect of the Enneagram
is that you can be a number

00:53:27.172 --> 00:53:30.230
with a wing and the wing isn't the number

00:53:30.230 --> 00:53:33.720
that is immediately adjacent
to each side of you.

00:53:33.720 --> 00:53:36.850
So I could be a three with a two wing

00:53:36.850 --> 00:53:38.290
or a three with a four wing,

00:53:38.290 --> 00:53:40.575
and you can also be a three
without a wing, right?

00:53:40.575 --> 00:53:42.800
But as the more I read about three,

00:53:42.800 --> 00:53:43.920
I'm definitely not a two.

00:53:43.920 --> 00:53:45.200
First of all, let me just say right now.

00:53:45.200 --> 00:53:48.490
Two, which is what my wife
is, which is a helper.

00:53:48.490 --> 00:53:49.520
And again, I think that's kind

00:53:49.520 --> 00:53:52.160
of a demeaning name to give to the two.

00:53:52.160 --> 00:53:54.700
There are better names
for it in other books.

00:53:54.700 --> 00:53:56.280
It makes it seem like
I'm just here to help.

00:53:56.280 --> 00:53:58.670
It just basically means that
they kind of give themselves

00:53:58.670 --> 00:54:01.520
to people in ways that
are just monumental.

00:54:01.520 --> 00:54:02.360
I'm not that.

00:54:02.360 --> 00:54:04.350
In fact, I score the lowest on two.

00:54:04.350 --> 00:54:05.530
Like if you look at my scores,

00:54:05.530 --> 00:54:07.250
like two is like barely ticking.

00:54:07.250 --> 00:54:10.190
But four, which is the individualist,

00:54:10.190 --> 00:54:11.600
I actually scored pretty high on,

00:54:11.600 --> 00:54:14.170
and a three with a four wing.

00:54:14.170 --> 00:54:15.470
This isn't let me, I'm going to read.

00:54:15.470 --> 00:54:17.236
This is from "Millenneagram."

00:54:17.236 --> 00:54:21.790
A three with a four wing
means that I'm most concerned

00:54:21.790 --> 00:54:24.890
with what I produce and
put out into the world.

00:54:24.890 --> 00:54:26.740
So that's where I found my value.

00:54:26.740 --> 00:54:29.000
It's not just necessarily like, hey,

00:54:29.000 --> 00:54:30.260
now again, it is like hey,

00:54:30.260 --> 00:54:31.093
we're doing this thing

00:54:31.093 --> 00:54:32.200
where we're throwing darts at a board.

00:54:32.200 --> 00:54:33.800
Well, I'm going to do the damnedest job

00:54:33.800 --> 00:54:35.500
I can possibly do in this game.

00:54:35.500 --> 00:54:36.540
That's why I'm so competitive

00:54:36.540 --> 00:54:37.920
in GMM in a lot of ways, right?

00:54:37.920 --> 00:54:39.480
Because you just put a challenge in front

00:54:39.480 --> 00:54:42.006
of me and I'm just like,
well, how do you win this?

00:54:42.006 --> 00:54:47.006
But really it manifests
itself in I am trying

00:54:48.858 --> 00:54:53.858
to find my worth in the
things that I produce, right?

00:54:55.550 --> 00:54:58.810
So what that ends up
doing is the net effect

00:54:58.810 --> 00:55:02.780
of that is every single
thing that we produce,

00:55:02.780 --> 00:55:06.130
every single thing that
we put out into the world,

00:55:06.130 --> 00:55:08.300
my self worth is attached to it.

00:55:08.300 --> 00:55:09.240
Now that's kind of true.

00:55:09.240 --> 00:55:11.940
You might say that's true
for all creative people.

00:55:11.940 --> 00:55:14.770
I believe that it is
true in a lot of ways.

00:55:14.770 --> 00:55:17.470
But it is fundamental to my core

00:55:17.470 --> 00:55:22.000
that I have been in this
long adulthood battle

00:55:22.000 --> 00:55:26.300
to detach my self worth from
the success of what we do.

00:55:26.300 --> 00:55:27.550
But that's my tendency.

00:55:27.550 --> 00:55:29.460
My tendency, and I think
that's one of the reasons

00:55:29.460 --> 00:55:30.730
that when I'm not healthy,

00:55:30.730 --> 00:55:32.210
I get so defensive.

00:55:32.210 --> 00:55:33.870
So we talked,

00:55:33.870 --> 00:55:36.220
you know last week or a
couple weeks ago about.

00:55:37.370 --> 00:55:38.203
- Failed projects.

00:55:38.203 --> 00:55:42.930
- GMM 22, the multi-episode
version of GMM.

00:55:42.930 --> 00:55:47.540
When it failed and when it
was in the midst of failing,

00:55:47.540 --> 00:55:49.150
when it was in the midst of getting

00:55:49.150 --> 00:55:52.760
this incredibly negative
reaction from fans,

00:55:52.760 --> 00:55:55.930
we decided that we were
going to do a podcast

00:55:55.930 --> 00:55:56.763
and talk about it.

00:55:56.763 --> 00:55:59.340
Now, we made the mistake
of just being like,

00:55:59.340 --> 00:56:00.720
we're just going to be real,

00:56:00.720 --> 00:56:03.743
and raw, and just process this live.

00:56:05.342 --> 00:56:07.690
I made an ass of myself
in a lot of ways, right?

00:56:07.690 --> 00:56:09.300
I was super defensive.

00:56:09.300 --> 00:56:13.120
I insulted people who
were disappointed in us.

00:56:13.120 --> 00:56:18.120
I was like a cornered dog, you know?

00:56:18.410 --> 00:56:21.290
I attacked and I lashed out.

00:56:21.290 --> 00:56:23.250
What I have come to understand

00:56:23.250 --> 00:56:28.150
is that I was defending my own worth.

00:56:28.150 --> 00:56:29.380
Not saying it was healthy.

00:56:29.380 --> 00:56:33.170
It was unhealthy because
I had so attached.

00:56:33.170 --> 00:56:37.090
I had identified my self-worth
with the success of the show.

00:56:37.090 --> 00:56:38.710
When people were rejecting the show,

00:56:38.710 --> 00:56:40.900
they weren't just rejecting me.

00:56:40.900 --> 00:56:43.810
They were telling me
that kind of worthless.

00:56:43.810 --> 00:56:45.490
Like you took this time,

00:56:45.490 --> 00:56:47.110
you hired all these people,

00:56:47.110 --> 00:56:49.990
you put all this thought
and effort into this thing.

00:56:49.990 --> 00:56:51.396
You know what?

00:56:51.396 --> 00:56:52.540
It's shit, man.

00:56:52.540 --> 00:56:53.470
That's what it is.

00:56:53.470 --> 00:56:55.718
It's the shittiest thing
you guys have ever done.

00:56:55.718 --> 00:56:58.123
So what I hear is you are shit.

00:56:59.610 --> 00:57:00.810
You're worthless.

00:57:00.810 --> 00:57:02.000
- Yeah.

00:57:02.000 --> 00:57:03.930
I may have told you that too, sorry.

00:57:03.930 --> 00:57:07.190
- So when I'm in the bad head space.

00:57:07.190 --> 00:57:09.110
Well first of all, should
have never made that podcast,

00:57:09.110 --> 00:57:10.210
I don't think.

00:57:10.210 --> 00:57:11.855
Maybe we learned something from it.

00:57:11.855 --> 00:57:14.150
But if I had to go back,

00:57:14.150 --> 00:57:15.495
I think there was a way to process

00:57:15.495 --> 00:57:20.495
that rejection in a healthy way

00:57:20.500 --> 00:57:22.150
but that wasn't what I did

00:57:22.150 --> 00:57:25.050
because I tied as a
three with a four wing,

00:57:25.050 --> 00:57:26.567
it's about the things that I bring to you.

00:57:26.567 --> 00:57:28.040
I'm like, here's something else.

00:57:28.040 --> 00:57:28.873
Here's something else.

00:57:28.873 --> 00:57:29.706
Here's a book.

00:57:29.706 --> 00:57:30.660
Here's a concert.

00:57:30.660 --> 00:57:33.640
Here's a song.

00:57:33.640 --> 00:57:34.560
You know what I'm saying?

00:57:34.560 --> 00:57:37.000
I'm constantly bringing
you things and you're,

00:57:37.000 --> 00:57:38.710
I'm like, am I worth something now?

00:57:38.710 --> 00:57:39.543
Is it okay?

00:57:39.543 --> 00:57:40.550
Am I enough now?

00:57:40.550 --> 00:57:41.383
Can I stop?

00:57:42.600 --> 00:57:44.130
That's the process that's going on.

00:57:44.130 --> 00:57:45.250
- And you know,

00:57:45.250 --> 00:57:48.030
they talk about the
emotional passion associated

00:57:48.030 --> 00:57:49.053
with each one.

00:57:50.023 --> 00:57:52.060
What is that for a three?

00:57:52.060 --> 00:57:53.640
- The emotional passion?

00:57:53.640 --> 00:57:54.970
- Yeah.

00:57:54.970 --> 00:57:58.210
For a one, it is anger.

00:57:58.210 --> 00:57:59.043
- Oh yeah.

00:57:59.043 --> 00:58:00.400
For a three it's deceit.

00:58:00.400 --> 00:58:01.830
- Okay, so does that,

00:58:01.830 --> 00:58:03.180
I don't know how that plays into this

00:58:03.180 --> 00:58:05.230
because to me it feels like the thing

00:58:05.230 --> 00:58:08.830
that I access is that okay,

00:58:08.830 --> 00:58:11.680
ones most often feel resentment,

00:58:11.680 --> 00:58:16.090
which is a kind of a low level
background tamped down anger

00:58:16.090 --> 00:58:18.770
that things aren't as they should be.

00:58:18.770 --> 00:58:20.400
So I try to remember,

00:58:20.400 --> 00:58:22.550
I don't remember what
I said in that podcast

00:58:22.550 --> 00:58:24.440
and how I was processing that.

00:58:24.440 --> 00:58:28.270
But I think that something
that had to be going on

00:58:28.270 --> 00:58:31.430
was just this frustration
that it didn't work

00:58:31.430 --> 00:58:33.240
and that I, I mean,

00:58:33.240 --> 00:58:36.710
my mind definitely goes back
to the things that we foresaw

00:58:36.710 --> 00:58:39.440
that we needed to work
in terms of the tool.

00:58:39.440 --> 00:58:41.744
Like, I start to blame how YouTube worked

00:58:41.744 --> 00:58:44.120
and we talked a lot about that because,

00:58:44.120 --> 00:58:48.200
and I fixated on that because
I felt like we had a plan

00:58:48.200 --> 00:58:52.170
and there's things that we
needed that didn't exist.

00:58:52.170 --> 00:58:56.100
It didn't work in a way to give
the audience the experience

00:58:56.100 --> 00:58:57.302
that I wanted.

00:58:57.302 --> 00:59:01.863
The perfect experience wasn't possible.

00:59:02.850 --> 00:59:07.470
When it became impossible
and it didn't pan out

00:59:07.470 --> 00:59:08.950
and didn't meet my standard,

00:59:08.950 --> 00:59:13.950
I just got very resentful and frustrated

00:59:14.080 --> 00:59:16.410
because there was there
was no way forward.

00:59:16.410 --> 00:59:21.410
It failed because it wasn't
going to come together.

00:59:21.570 --> 00:59:22.784
